From: Bogdan Mircea <mirceapetrebogdan@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] types: free untracked values during garbage collection

The retain phase defers freeing GC-linked values until the second pass so
its list traversal stays valid. A value with an unused ref field has no
second-pass entry; retaining it after its last reference is dropped leaks
its allocation.

Free those untracked values immediately. In particular, older binary modules
can still register off-pool resource prototypes through the public API even
when rebuilt inline helpers put prototypes in the VM pool. Preserve that
compatibility without moving values between VM owners or changing the ABI.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Bogdan Mircea <mirceapetrebogdan@gmail.com>
---

--- a/types.c
+++ b/types.c
@@ -375,7 +375,8 @@ ucv_free(uc_value_t *uv, bool retain)
 		break;
 	}
 
-	if (!ref || !retain) {
+	/* Only linked values have a second GC pass to reclaim their storage. */
+	if (!ref || !ref->next || !retain) {
 		if (ref && ref->prev && ref->next)
 			ucv_unref(ref);
 
